{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 4"},"body":"Pinned source statements support the following navigation links.\n\nInspected: Configured challenge assertions, their relevant definitions and the cited audited paper statements were compared.","content_sha256":"sha256:045c5bbd17793cd457297a06584b9e2a55f36e912309552d20cd33d2e70d0c39","fingerprint":"sha256:65a22f5bbaca679c54229cb8244eeb2b6512e37e618c73b9d2bf2119de13a0f9","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Pinned source statements support the following navigation links.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:f72d9643f0dab3bdb18876f54b072f9720fc99491e3801f2a46214e90f7e2e50","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.BinPackingGap.main_results"],"explanation":"The first formal conjunct constructs rational item sizes above 1/6 with both individual and type configuration LP value B but optimum exceeding B+c for every c. This is the unbounded-gap theorem; the formal statement additionally fixes the construction size to 5B. The other formal conjuncts concern hardness and algorithms, so this is one source component rather than the entire formal assertion.","fingerprint":"sha256:9db6d23acbb0d0d9b3e8ed09415491fc6b0d222a9e448dbdae3e81c25b7ed830","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Additive-hardness-and-unbounded-configuration-gaps-in-bin-packing-September-24-2026#thm:unbounded-gap","statement_sha256":"sha256:f0d4c23a21b80f2e2d6f04acbbc984221585dd936c2b69e35a969ace0b7d9c9a"},{"declarations":["OAI.BinPackingGap.main_results"],"explanation":"The PackingGapNPHard conjunct states NP-hardness of the additive B versus B+c packing distinction. The additive-hardness theorem makes that distinction for rational instances with sizes above 1/6. It supplies the hardness component, separate from the fractional-gap construction and the algorithm equivalence.","fingerprint":"sha256:8663b2b3790a601e0ca27afdfdbb940b169358120d9a04e8f0e9ff5af848f848","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Additive-hardness-and-unbounded-configuration-gaps-in-bin-packing-September-24-2026#thm:additive-hardness","statement_sha256":"sha256:47da669061a883c68f05927fa2ea3c30aaa92ee324c4eb768107fb2450ef7085"},{"declarations":["OAI.BinPackingGap.main_results"],"explanation":"The formal assertion includes existence of an absolute-additive polynomial-time packing algorithm if and only if P equals NP. That is the complexity-equivalence corollary. The formal theorem also specifies exact output, empty input and invalid-input behavior under P=NP; those additional implementation clauses are not asserted by this corollary.","fingerprint":"sha256:936bc5f1efd8153475ee035b186f3625d5028da9b946ddb66cf08426ade4a87c","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Additive-hardness-and-unbounded-configuration-gaps-in-bin-packing-September-24-2026#cor:complexity-equiv","statement_sha256":"sha256:6aeb86a3f53734e36ed6615ff72afa784f082bb82136522ce851449c259bd182"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/BinPackingGap.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Additive-hardness-and-unbounded-configuration-gaps-in-bin-packing-September-24-2026/build/source/introduction.tex#L87","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Additive-hardness-and-unbounded-configuration-gaps-in-bin-packing-September-24-2026/build/source/introduction.tex#L106","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Additive-hardness-and-unbounded-configuration-gaps-in-bin-packing-September-24-2026/build/source/introduction.tex#L114"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:BinPackingGap","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/6064027622f4e5b5ec30fff0.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/6064027622f4e5b5ec30fff0.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/6064027622f4e5b5ec30fff0.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/6064027622f4e5b5ec30fff0.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/6064027622f4e5b5ec30fff0.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.BinPackingGap.main_results","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/BinPackingGap.lean","line":356,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"f72d9643f0dab3bdb18876f54b072f9720fc99491e3801f2a46214e90f7e2e50","statement_sha256":"sha256:805b287bad7191547f5607998589488d82b007e1d50c00221d5d3ef997dc672a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/BinPackingGap.lean#L356"},"text":"theorem main_results :\n    (∀ c : ℕ, ∃ I : Instance, ∃ B : ℕ,\n      I.n = 5 * B ∧\n      (∀ i, (1 / 6 : ℚ) < I.size i ∧ I.size i < 1) ∧\n      B + c < opt I ∧ individualLP I = (B : ℝ) ∧ typeLP I = (B : ℝ)) ∧\n    (∀ c : Nat, PackingGapNPHard c) ∧\n    ((∃ c : Nat, Nonempty (AbsoluteAdditiveAlgorithm c)) ↔ PEqualsNP) ∧\n    (PEqualsNP → ∃ algorithm : AbsoluteAdditiveAlgorithm 0,\n    (∀ (items : RawInstance) (valid : items.Valid), ∃ packing : RawPacking,\n      algorithm.run (BinaryEncoding.rawInstanceBits items) = some packing ∧\n      packing.Feasible items ∧ packing.bins = opt (items.toInstance valid)) ∧\n    algorithm.run (BinaryEncoding.rawInstanceBits []) = some ⟨0, []⟩ ∧\n    (∀ input : List Bool, BinaryEncoding.decodeRawInstance input = none →\n      algorithm.run input = none) ∧\n    (∀ items : RawInstance, ¬ items.Valid →\n      algorithm.run (BinaryEncoding.rawInstanceBits items) = none))"}],"state":"available","unresolved_names":[]},"generation_id":"sha256:c701139844a2d825c371ded7486924e7dae7de0af77a69dc9c1abaf1129191a1","id":"l:BinPackingGap","kind":"lean-preview","omissions":[],"pairings":{"f:118":{"alternatives":[],"contributed_readings":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 4"},"content_sha256":"sha256:045c5bbd17793cd457297a06584b9e2a55f36e912309552d20cd33d2e70d0c39","decision":"linked","detail":{"path":"lean-previews/6064027622f4e5b5ec30fff0.json","pointer":"/contributions/0"},"provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"review_state":"unreviewed","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.BinPackingGap.main_results"],"limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","target":"r:Additive-hardness-and-unbounded-configuration-gaps-in-bin-packing-September-24-2026:thm:unbounded-gap"},{"declarations":["OAI.BinPackingGap.main_results"],"limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","target":"r:Additive-hardness-and-unbounded-configuration-gaps-in-bin-packing-September-24-2026:thm:additive-hardness"},{"dec